      "alerts": [
        {
          "event": "Red Flag Warning",
          "headline": "Red Flag Warning issued August 27 at 10:46PM PDT until August 28 at 3:00PM PDT by NWS San Francisco CA",
          "severity": "Severe",
          "urgency": "Expected",
          "description": "...RED FLAG WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT FROM 5 AM TO 3 PM PDT FRIDAY\nDUE TO LIGHTNING FOR SANTA CRUZ MOUNTAINS, SOUTHERN SALINAS\nVALLEY/ARROYO SECO AND LAKE SAN ANTONIO, SANTA LUCIA MOUNTAINS AND\nLOS PADRES NATIONAL FOREST, NORTHERN SALINAS VALLEY/HOLLISTER VALLEY\nAND CARMEL VALLEY, NORTHERN MONTEREY BAY, AND SOUTHERN MONTEREY BAY\nAND BIG SUR COAST...\n\n....The potential for isolated thunderstorms across the Central Coast\ncontinues to increase from Friday morning through Friday afternoon...\n\n* AFFECTED AREA...The Salinas and Carmel Valleys and Hollister Area,\nMonterey Bay and the Big Sur Coast, The Santa Cruz Mountains, and\nInterior Monterey County and the Santa Lucia Range.\n\n* TIMING...From 5 AM to 3 PM PDT Friday.\n\n* THUNDERSTORMS...Lightning strikes with little precipitation and\ngusty and erratic outflow winds of 40 to 50 mph.\n\n* IMPACTS...There will be an increased risk for power outages.\nLightning strikes may result in new fire ignitions. Erratic outflow\nwinds will result in rapid fire spread for both new and existing\nfires.",
          "instruction": "Please advise responding agencies or fire crews in the field of this\nfire weather alert.\n\nNever leave burning debris or camp fires unattended; extinguish them\ncompletely. Avoid using equipment or machinery that could create a\nspark. Secure tow chains to avoid dragging and subsequent sparks.\nNever toss cigarette butts out of your vehicle's window. Remember,\none less spark, one less flame.\n\nFamiliarize yourself with your emergency plan! Where will you go? How\nwill you get there? Do you have your go kit ready to go? Who will you\ncall to let others know you are safe? Visit ready.gov/plan for more\ninformation.",
          "expires": "2026-08-28T08:00:00-07:00",
          "source_url": "https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.277a37b03762bc2528fdd877c1d251b6b8f7edaf.001.1"
        }
      ]
    },
